 SPEC CONFORMANCE (Fluent / WinUI 3 guidelines)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 nav            : ShellWindow PageFactory.Register("SignalLogViewer", ...); RouteTable deep-link /signal-log
 scaffold       : SignalLogViewerPage : UserControl + SignalLogViewerPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged
                  (CommunityToolkit-style observable holder); LoadAsync()/RefreshAsync()/QueryAsync();
                  zero business logic in code-behind (thin renderer over SignalLogViewerDisplay projection)
 panels/tokens  : Mica/Acrylic TsGlassPanel; design-token brushes (TsColor*Brush) via TypographyTokens —
                  no hardcoded colors/typography (PageTitle/Subhead/PanelTitle/Caption roles)
 data states    : loading (TsPageLoadSkeleton) / empty (TsEmptyState) / error (TsAlertBanner) / success
                  for the useSignals source; + faithful results region (TsTableSkeleton / TsDataTable /
                  TsEmptyState) for the deferred history read
 i18n           : every string via ILocalizer + .resw, web key names preserved (ADR-014)
 a11y           : AutomationProperties.SetName on page/picker/controls/panels; FontIcons marked
                  AccessibilityView.Raw; keyboard + pointer through native Fluent controls (ADR-015)
 units          : SI read straight from the API; values formatted at the display boundary
                  (DateTimeFormatting) — no non-SI stored/computed (P1/S5)
 reuse          : shared SignalSelector feature-view reused (not re-implemented)

